{
  "comment": "Adoption Ledger — factory defaults a real product must own. Hashes are SHA-256 of shipped bytes (raw file content on disk — a CRLF checkout would flip every hash and green the whole ledger on day zero; .gitattributes ships \"* text=auto eol=lf\" repo-wide to prevent that). Status is an AND rule per item, not per file: an item is \"factory-default\" if ANY of its listed files is still present with a matching hash (one untouched shipped file means the item is not yet owned); \"removed\" only when ALL listed files are missing; otherwise \"touched\" — note a trivial edit or a formatter pass is enough to flip an item to touched; that's accepted, since the ledger only guides adopters to the right skill, and the per-item recipes (not the hash check) are what actually gate production readiness. Regenerate with: pnpm factory:manifest (template repo only, gated by .factory/config.json having \"template\": true).",
